<title>AUSTRALIA: Cricket-Pakistan slump to be all out for 149 in 46th over.</title>
<headline>Cricket-Pakistan slump to be all out for 149 in 46th over.</headline>
<dateline>HOBART 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aggressive bowling and a series of run-outs saw Pakistan slump to be all out for 149 in the 46th over of its one-day match against Australia in Hobart on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Rookie fast-bowler Andrew Bichel starred for Australia, taking three for 17 off his ten overs including two of Pakistan's three opening batsmen for ducks in his first two overs.</p>
